Theorem 1.6 (`th:main3`): for every set Γ, ℓ₁(Γ,L₁[0,1]) has UPFP;
consequently C[0,1]* has UPFP and is primary. Γ is an arbitrary type,
with no cardinality, countability or nonemptiness assumption.
